From 2654be578d9c80f1fefaf9f50a9b41e5de0e3a56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:53:06 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/53] sysfs: give md the new data offset of a reshape that
 goes on

A reshape that changes data_offset continues after a restart only if md
gets each device's new_offset before the array starts: md otherwise
takes new_offset = offset and goes on reshaping onto the data it has not
moved yet.  sysfs_set_array() sets reshape_position, raid_disks, layout
and chunk_size, but nothing sets new_offset for the external metadata
that assemble through sysfs_add_disk().

Write it when the array is being reshaped and the metadata gives a
new_data_offset that differs - AMD RAIDXpert2 (later in this series)
moves the data of each member 0x4800 sectors down -, after "size": md
refuses a size for a device whose offset changes.  No other metadata
gives a new_data_offset from container_content(), so IMSM, DDF and
native arrays assemble as before.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 sysfs.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sysfs.c b/sysfs.c
index 2597fb02..1f14507f 100644
--- a/sysfs.c
+++ b/sysfs.c
@@ -1065,6 +1065,16 @@ int sysfs_add_disk(struct mdinfo *sra, struct mdinfo *sd, int resume)
 
 	rv = sysfs_set_num(sra, sd, "offset", sd->data_offset);
 	rv |= sysfs_set_num(sra, sd, "size", (sd->component_size+1) / 2);
+	/*
+	 * A reshape that moves the data (external metadata records where to:
+	 * new_data_offset) goes on only with the offset it moves them to -
+	 * else md would go on with new_offset = offset, over data not moved
+	 * yet.  After "size": md takes no size for a device whose offset
+	 * changes.
+	 */
+	if (sra->reshape_active && sd->new_data_offset &&
+	    sd->new_data_offset != sd->data_offset)
+		rv |= sysfs_set_num(sra, sd, "new_offset", sd->new_data_offset);
 	if (!is_container(sra->array.level)) {
 		if (sra->consistency_policy == CONSISTENCY_POLICY_PPL) {
 			rv |= sysfs_set_num(sra, sd, "ppl_sector", sd->ppl_sector);
